WEBVTT

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.310
I feel the same for Tatsumi too.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.110
He also has his way of thinking.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:17.080
Using that kind of game to determine the starting line-up.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.910
I feel that Tatsumi is that kind of a person.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.330
Though it's only my feelings.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.260
Dori...

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.260
I still have something to ask you.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.180
We will now also conduct a competition to determine the starting line-up.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:45.900
Again?

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.730
That was only a reference.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.030
The end product is not everything.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.280
That's about all I can take...

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:57.910
Hey, Kuro!

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:04.120
This is bad. It's no joke. Things really are turning for the worse.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.170
Those who don't feel like playing the next match are allowed to not participate.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.670
However, those who want to win the next game...

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.680
Go ahead and enjoy the competition!

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.070
Damn...

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.970
There's no need for you to skip training together with me.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:26.010
You'll get fined and banned from playing. Banned!

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.140
There won't be any appearance bonuses for you too.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.560
Money's not the issue here.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:36.020
It's not being able to play that is so much more unbearable.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.410
That asshole...

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:48.410
The opening match of the Japan Cup is such a big game! Doesn't he want to win?

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:55.420
Though I'm nothing compared to Koshi, but I have always wanted this team to win.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.960
And I give my all.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.430
I'm neither as tall as you nor good in techniques,

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.390
Which is why I compensate with guts and an undying attitude to snatch the ball.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.640
I have always played with these qualities in order to be an integral member of the squad.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.690
I know.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:19.690
Though we've had a number of inept managers before,

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:27.330
I have never actually seen one who would bring off players who wanted to win just because he doesn't like them!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.120
What's with him? He startled me.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:39.800
Calm down, Kuro.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.220
I admire that hot, passionate side of yours.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:53.230
A combative player such as you will surely be a threat to any opponent.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:57.400
You are a player that no manager would say they wouldn't need.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.230
I was just speaking the truth.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:01.730
Alright, hear me out.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.030
I approached Dori for his opinions.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:06.950
Of what?

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.080
I asked him about the previous match that we were not called up for,

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.000
As well as the match before that.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:17.630
How does he feel about being protected by two different defensive pairings?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.880
How I felt?

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.130
Yes.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:30.890
Well, the decision was a sudden one,

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.140
Therefore there were certain risks.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:35.640
However,

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.650
Those youngsters did produce the desired effects.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.150
Conversely, when you two were up there,

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.700
It just feels like time has stopped for you.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.620
The team is moving forward, yet the two of you lagging behind. Is that fine with you?

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:07.300
I don't have a clue about what you're saying!

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.630
Kuro...

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.760
As I expected...

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:52.090
The problem lies in our defense line.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:56.890
You're still going on with that? Didn't I mention that our performance was fine!

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.520
When we were needed in offense, we helped out too!

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.270
Don't keep harping on what Akasaki said, Sugi!

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.990
The difference was that the team was unable to score in the two matches that we've played in.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.910
In addition, Sera even scored during the previous game.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:19.620
Both the games ended with losses, but they were able to defend, as well as play better.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.800
Though Kobayashi and Kamei were worried about the opponents breaking through,

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.760
They still kept a high line...

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:37.520
This narrows down the space we expose in the midfield area, while allowing us to assist with simple passes.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.110
This heightens our attacking prowess.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.150
And we're able to create more chances.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:54.740
It's Gino!

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.250
Tsubaki!

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:02.960
You can do it!

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.510
Your decision-making's too slow, Tsubaki!

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:16.930
Beware of their counter!

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.140
Damn it!

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.390
What happened, Baki?

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.190
You fell for the same trick back there.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:26.650
I'm sorry.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.150
Two more men! Cover up!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:32.780
Geez, your ignorance made you look like a cute idiot.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:39.740
Still can't get over your mistakes during the pre-season game?

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:53.550
That's not it!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:09:04.390
Well, anyway, I don't have much patience for a dog that I have to constantly spoon-feed. Understood?

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:16.660
I must stop giving the team any more troubles!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.580
I need to do something. Anything!

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.750
He was almost through, and yet...

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.050
Guess he's still not up to it, that Tsubaki.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.590
Just let him be.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.090
It's not like I expected much from him.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:43.470
Just let him find his own answers on the pitch.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.560
We'll just take it as we go.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.730
Right now, the real problem is that side.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:57.820
Will Kobayashi and Kamei grab their chances?

00:09:58.910 --> 00:09:59.620
Or,

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:09.580
Will the two rebels be able to find their own answers off the pitch?

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:19.180
How will things develop? Time's almost up.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.860
Ever since Tatsumi took over as manager,

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.450
This team has started to change.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:45.620
All he did was change the line-up of the team, though the way we approach the game is still the same,

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:50.210
And this team has played even better than before.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.960
During the match against Victory, we were playing well for a period of time,

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.470
You would've noticed it too, Kuro.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.470
That first goal during the opening game,

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:09.350
We cowered and dropped off from that initial shot.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:10.730
What?

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.940
That was only a lucky goal.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.400
We should've forgotten about it right after that.

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:18.940
Instead...

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:25.450
We became uneasy and stuck ourselves in front of goal.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.120
Just like what we did last year.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.420
That's not it! We were just...

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:39.420
We only had it in our heads, but our bodies didn't carry it out.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:45.890
I looked over from the bench during the last game...

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:52.020
I noticed that Dori positioned himself further up than before.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:58.480
He had lots of opportunities to take control of the ball in the penalty area,

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:03.910
This is evidence that the defense line has been pushed up.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:08.160
This team is gradually moving forward,

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:12.710
Yet, both of us are remained in our comfort zone, which in turn, exposed the space in front of us.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:19.880
It's exactly like what the manager, coach, Akasaki and Dori said.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.590
We didn't change at all.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.180
We only thought that we changed.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:29.890
So what now, Kuro?

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:34.480
If this goes on, our position will be taken away by the youngsters!

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:45.530
Though the manager has changed, the players are still in the same formation.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.540
The initial opponents that we have to defeat...

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:52.790
...is not the opposing teams.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.330
It's ourselves.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:01.300
This team's 'losing culture'...

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.720
...runs deep into the veins.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:22.400
If the players can't understand the manager's decision to rotate them after a game, they won't last the season.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:35.910
Rotation? So that was your objective when you organized that game competition?

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:38.250
Didn't I tell you?

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.880
I've never heard that before! Not once!

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:45.510
Why do you tell us these important details only after everything's done?

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:52.890
N-No way!

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:54.640
A penalty?

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:19.380
Though Kamei's marking was tight, he was a little too eager.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.000
Dori.

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:23.880
It's all up to you.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.430
Dori...

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:38.480
It's been two years since we last played together...

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.060
I'm a bit reluctant.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:47.650
Dori...

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:58.660
It's saved!

00:14:59.000 --> 00:14:59.920
The follow-up!

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:02.290
Kamei!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.750
Stop him!

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.800
We were so close!

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.560
I'm sorry, Dori...

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:29.110
Forget about it! We need to score!

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.290
Don't let your heads down! Defend from the front!

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:43.790
Dori...

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.000
This cannot happen again.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:51.010
We shouldn't embarrass Dori anymore.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:54.260
Kuro...

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:01.850
We'll have to give it a shot, damn it.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.200
Is that so?

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.910
That's not good! Bye then.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:23.250
Who was that?

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.500
It's the grocery store owner. He called for an order.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:30.170
He then went to watch a soccer game.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:32.220
But they lost again!

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.130
ETU.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:38.010
It's been so many years, and they are still such a weak team!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.970
Dear, I thought you weren't interested in soccer?

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:46.190
I'm still not interested, but it's only natural that I want the local team to win!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:47.810
Here! Thanks for waiting!

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.860
Enjoy your food!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.700
Let's finish this up quickly and leave.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.280
Old man, your ramen is fantastic! Though I wasn't so sure initially...

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.580
So are you complimenting me or dissing me?

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:03.830
Whatever, I'll forgive you.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.830
What an annoying old man.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:12.510
Well, I have been honing my skills for the past fifty years.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:16.510
Compared to other stores, my pair of hands is certainly different from theirs!

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:20.390
Fifty years? That's amazing!

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:23.430
It's quite a feat that your business could last that long.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:26.730
You have thorns in your words again.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:32.110
Well, there were ups and downs from time to time; it's important to look at the bright side of things.

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:36.240
If you've failed to produce a good bowl of ramen, you just have to try again.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:39.200
If you failed today, just try again tomorrow!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.200
So we should just forget about our failures?

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.870
That's right! Just forget about them!

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.210
Forget!

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:51.960
Getting depressed isn't the way to go. All you need is to take it easy!

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:55.090
The two gentlemen over there look quite capable. Wanna take over my shop?

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:57.590
Thanks for your patronage!

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.640
My ears are producing wax just from listening to his lecture.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.020
Who would wanna go back?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:25.910
Alright.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.460
We lost again yesterday.

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.300
Are you still going to play that childish game?

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.270
So you're interested?

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:48.350
Of course not, dammit! It's not like I'm doing it for your sake!

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:52.690
I just hate losing to someone! You understand?

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:53.770
Kuro...

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:54.820
You're going overboard.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:01.450
W-What? Say something.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:06.830
No matter how good a strategy is, if you can't have possession of the ball, it's still all talk.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.750
Football starts from its defense.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.960
Therefore, ETU's football starts from the two of you.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:30.350
I'm expecting great things from you, defense team!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:48.580
We can do it!

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:52.250
Long ball!

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:53.500
No.9, Kia!

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:57.920
He's not wearing down at all!

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:00.760
What? It's alright. He's starting to wear out.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.510
Don't commit a foul again, Kuro!

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:09.770
What's that? I wasn't being impulsive at all!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:13.230
Okay, nice one, Kuro! Nice clear!

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.650
That was close!

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:17.270
He was panicking.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:27.280
Looks like he's finally listening. And he was also participating in the Soccer-Tennis game!

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:32.460
The defense is solid today. Our game is finally coming together!

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:36.750
Both Kuroda and Sugi are really concentrating.

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:43.880
That said though, the problem now is whether or not they can maintain their performance if anything bad were to happen.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.760
You can say so, but we've done all we can, Macchan.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.770
The only thing we can do now...

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.100
...is to believe in them.

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:20.960
Is that all you've got? You guys can do better than that!

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:24.590
We can't lose today! Cheer louder!

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.970
Set-pieces. This is where we really need to be focusing hard!

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:34.730
Spread out! Spread out!

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.980
Mark your man!

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:42.480
You guys be careful! We've been playing well since the start!

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:48.240
It's into the box!

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:49.990
Mine!

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:10.140
How can we concede at this kind of time? Damn it!

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:18.560
I screwed up.

00:22:18.850 --> 00:22:20.400
I was supposed to mark him!

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:22.150
Ishihama!

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:25.860
Don't let your head down! We're only starting!

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:30.280
That was due to a set play, not a breakdown in our defense!

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:33.910
Come on, walk with your heads held high!

00:22:33.910 --> 00:22:34.160
Yes!
Come on, walk with your heads held high!

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:34.200
Yes!

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:38.870
Alright! That's the way!

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:41.710
You've become a capable team!

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:48.220
Let's pull it back! Our defense's not conceding another!

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:18.310
Is it because of me that we can't win?

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:20.680
We'll meet up ten minutes later at Gate W-1!

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:22.770
Bad news! The fans...

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:24.520
Just wait and see, Nagoya!

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:26.060
I'm going to smash you to bits!

00:24:26.770 --> 00:24:28.190
Pepe!
